# Half-Life shotgun (SPAS-12). Measured by vrcardgen, finished by hand.
#
# The one moving part is the fore-end, bone "Charger", travelling 3.42 units
# along Y. It is animated only in `shoot` and `shoot_big` - Half-Life pumps
# the gun as part of firing rather than in a sequence of its own - but the
# travel is the travel, and once a hand owns it the animation is irrelevant.
#
# A tube gun is the best possible first card: it needs no magazine, and this
# model has no magazine bone. Shells go in through the gate one at a time,
# which is a gesture the hands can already make.

weapon v_shotgun
match  bones 56  seqs 8  hash 0xbf9fd5e8

# The bone every position in this card is measured in - the controls, the
# grab points, the chamber, the ejection port. Nothing recorded it until
# the engine had to place a control in the world to ask whether a thumb is
# near it; the simulator never needed one, because it never works in world
# space. Taken from the generator, which has always called this bone the
# WEAPON BODY and is what measured these numbers in the first place.
body   "Reciever"

type   tube_pump  capacity 8  rpm 75

joint 0  bone "Charger"  slide  travel 3.42  rest 0
    grab  point 0.00 -13.31 0.00  radius 3.0

# The feed and ejection points keep the preset's positions. Where in the
# stroke a shell actually leaves has NOT been measured, and inventing a
# number would be worse than using one that is honestly a default.
